# DiariZen (wavlm-large-s80-md-v2) as TorchScript — {VARIANT} build

**Non-commercial use only (CC BY-NC 4.0).** This is a format conversion made for
[FineSub](https://github.com/caca2331/finesub)'s speaker diarization, so it can run without the
`diarizen` and `pyannote.audio` packages. It is **not** a new model and was **not** retrained.

| File | What it is | From | Licence |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `diarizen_segmentation.ts` | WavLM-Large (pruned) + Conformer local segmentation, traced forward pass | [BUT-FIT/diarizen-wavlm-large-s80-md-v2](https://huggingface.co/BUT-FIT/diarizen-wavlm-large-s80-md-v2) @ `027b3e22` | CC BY-NC 4.0 |
| `diarizen_embedding.ts` | WeSpeaker ResNet34 speaker-embedding network (the part after fbank), traced | [pyannote/wespeaker-voxceleb-resnet34-LM](https://huggingface.co/pyannote/wespeaker-voxceleb-resnet34-LM) @ `837717dd` | CC BY 4.0 |
| `plda/plda.npz`, `plda/xvec_transform.npz` | PLDA and x-vector transform, copied unchanged | BUT-FIT/diarizen-wavlm-large-s80-md-v2 | CC BY-NC 4.0 |

The bundle carries the most restrictive of the three: **CC BY-NC 4.0**.

## {VARIANT} only

TorchScript records the device it was traced on. These files were traced on **{DEVICE}** and run
only on {DEVICE}; the {OTHER} build is [{OTHER_REPO}]({OTHER_REPO_URL}).

## What changed from the originals

- Traced with `torch.jit.trace` (torch {TORCH}); not frozen, not quantised, weights unchanged.
- The traced modules were checked against the eager originals bit for bit, repeated calls at batch
  sizes 1–3, before writing.
- Everything else DiariZen does — windowing, powerset decoding, VBx clustering — is reimplemented
  in FineSub; see its documentation for how that port was characterised.

Export script: `tools/diarizen_export/export_diarizen.py` in the FineSub repository.

## Credit

DiariZen is by BUT Speech@FIT. Please cite their work (see the
[original model card](https://huggingface.co/BUT-FIT/diarizen-wavlm-large-s80-md-v2)) and the
WeSpeaker paper (Wang et al., ICASSP 2023) for the embedding model. Some of DiariZen's training
data is research-only, which is why its weights — and therefore this conversion — may not be used
commercially.
